    {
      "card_id": "card_33_refraction_intro",
      "card_slug": "card_33_refraction_intro",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "refraction_intro",
      "level": 4,
      "progress": {
        "current": 33,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Raju, agar tum paani se bhari baalti mein ek pencil tedi karke rakho, toh pencil tedhi dikhti hai - broken jaisi!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Haan Sir! Aur swimming pool mein apne pair chhote lagte hain!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Perfect examples! Ye hota hai Refraction - jab light ek medium se dusre medium (different density) mein jaati hai toh uski direction CHANGE ho jati hai aur speed bhi change hoti hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Matlab reflection mein toh direction change hoti thi lekin medium same tha, refraction mein medium change hota hai?"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_34_refraction_cause",
        "button_text": "Cause Samjho ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_34_refraction_cause",
      "card_slug": "card_34_refraction_cause",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "refraction_cause",
      "level": 4,
      "progress": {
        "current": 34,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Bilkul sahi! Refraction ka basic cause hai - change in speed of light when medium changes. Light vacuum mein fastest (3 × 10⁸ m/s), denser medium (glass, water) mein slow ho jati hai. Speed change hone se direction bend hoti hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Toh glass mein light kitni slow ho jati hai?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Ye measure karte hain REFRACTIVE INDEX se! Refractive index (n) = Speed of light in vacuum (c) / Speed of light in medium (v). Glass ka n ≈ 1.5, paani ka n ≈ 1.33, diamond ka highest n ≈ 2.42! Jitna zyada n, utna zyada denser medium!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Matlab diamond mein light sabse zyada slow hoti hai isliye itna sparkle karta hai?"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_35_refractive_index",
        "button_text": "Refractive Index ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_35_refractive_index",
      "card_slug": "card_35_refractive_index",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "refractive_index_detail",
      "level": 4,
      "progress": {
        "current": 35,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Exactly! Diamond ki high refractive index ki wajah se total internal reflection zyada hota hai - isliye brilliance! Important: Refractive index ek RATIO hai, dimensionless hai (no unit). Air ka n ≈ 1 (reference), vacuum ka exactly 1."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Sir, toh agar light rarer se denser mein jaye toh kya hoga?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Golden Rule: Rarer to Denser → Light BENDS TOWARDS the normal (angle of refraction < angle of incidence). Denser to Rarer → Light BENDS AWAY FROM the normal (angle of refraction > angle of incidence). ⭐ BPSC/NEET Favorite Trap - Direction of bending!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Matlab air se paani mein jane pe normal ki taraf bend, paani se air mein jane pe normal se door bend!"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_36_laws_of_refraction",
        "button_text": "Laws Seekho ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_36_laws_of_refraction",
      "card_slug": "card_36_laws_of_refraction",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "laws_refraction",
      "level": 4,
      "progress": {
        "current": 36,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Perfect! Ab laws of refraction: FIRST LAW - Incident ray, refracted ray aur normal teenon same plane mein hote hain. SECOND LAW (SNELL'S LAW) - n₁ sin i = n₂ sin r. Jahan n₁ = refractive index of first medium, i = angle of incidence, n₂ = refractive index of second medium, r = angle of refraction."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Ye Snell's Law ka naam kiska naam pe hai Sir?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Willebrord Snellius (Dutch scientist, 1621). ⭐ UPSC/BPSC Favorite - Scientist name questions! Snell's Law se hi refractive index calculate karte hain. Agar air (n=1) se glass (n=1.5) mein light 30° pe incident ho, toh sin 30° = 0.5, toh 1 × 0.5 = 1.5 × sin r → sin r = 0.33 → r ≈ 19.5°"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Toh angle chota ho gaya - normal ki taraf bend hua!"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_37_real_life_refraction",
        "button_text": "Real Life Examples ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_37_real_life_refraction",
      "card_slug": "card_37_real_life_refraction",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "refraction_examples",
      "level": 4,
      "progress": {
        "current": 37,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Refraction ke daily life effects: (1) Pool mein depth kam dikhna - apparent depth < real depth. (2) Coin paani mein rakhne pe upar uthta dikhna. (3) Stars twinkling - atmospheric refraction. (4) Sun sunrise se pehle aur sunset ke baad dikhna - atmospheric refraction. (5) Mirage in deserts!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Matlab sun actually ufaq (horizon) ke neeche hai lekin refraction ki wajah se dikhai deta hai?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Exactly! Sunrise 2 minutes early aur sunset 2 minutes late dikhta hai refraction ki wajah se - total 4 minutes extra sunlight! ⭐ BPSC/UPSC Statement Favorite! Atmosphere ki layers ki density alag hoti hai toh light continuously bend hoti rehti hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Aur twinkling?"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_38_twinkling_stars",
        "button_text": "Twinkling Samjho ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_38_twinkling_stars",
      "card_slug": "card_38_twinkling_stars",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "twinkling_explanation",
      "level": 4,
      "progress": {
        "current": 38,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Twinkling of stars hoti hai kyunki star light jab atmosphere mein aati hai, changing air density layers se multiple refractions hoti hai. Since atmosphere constantly moving hai (turbulence), path change hota rehta hai - kabhi bright, kabhi dim - twinkling effect!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Lekin Sir, planets twinkle kyun nahi karte?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Brilliant question! ⭐ NEET/BPSC Favorite Trap! Stars are point sources (bahut door), so slight path change = brightness change dikhta hai. Planets extended sources hain (closer, bigger angular size), multiple points se light aati hai toh averaging effect hota hai - twinkling cancel out ho jati hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Wow! Isliye planets steady light dete hain!"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_39_tir_intro",
        "button_text": "Next Phenomenon ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_39_tir_intro",
      "card_slug": "card_39_tir_intro",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "tir_intro",
      "level": 4,
      "progress": {
        "current": 39,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Ab aata hai refraction ka sabse amazing phenomenon - TOTAL INTERNAL REFLECTION (TIR)! Jab light denser medium se rarer medium mein jati hai aur angle of incidence ek critical value se zyada ho, toh light refract na hokar COMPLETELY REFLECT ho jati hai back into denser medium!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Matlab kuch conditions mein refraction nahi, reflection hota hai?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Haan! Do conditions zaroori hain TIR ke liye: (1) Light must travel from DENSER to RARER medium. (2) Angle of incidence must be GREATER than Critical Angle. Critical Angle (C) wo angle hai jiske liye angle of refraction = 90°!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Agar 90° se zyada ho jaye toh?"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_40_critical_angle",
        "button_text": "Critical Angle ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_40_critical_angle",
      "card_slug": "card_40_critical_angle",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "critical_angle",
      "level": 4,
      "progress": {
        "current": 40,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Jab angle of incidence critical angle se zyada ho jaye, refraction possible nahi (kyunki angle of refraction 90° se zyada nahi ho sakta), toh sari light reflect ho jati hai - Total Internal Reflection! Formula: sin C = n₂/n₁ = 1/n (agar second medium air hai). Glass-Air interface ke liye C ≈ 42°, Water-Air ke liye C ≈ 49°."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Matlab glass mein agar light 42° se zyada angle pe surface pe hit kare toh reflect ho jayegi?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Perfect! ⭐ NEET/BPSC Formula Favorite! TIR applications: (1) Diamond ka sparkle - low critical angle (≈24°) due to high n. (2) Optical fibres - internet, endoscopy. (3) Mirage - hot road pe inverted image. (4) Prisms in binoculars!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Sir mirage kaise banta hai?"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_41_mirage_explanation",
        "button_text": "Mirage Samjho ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_41_mirage_explanation",
      "card_slug": "card_41_mirage_explanation",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "mirage",
      "level": 4,
      "progress": {
        "current": 41,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Garmi mein road bahut hot ho jati hai, uske paas ki air layer bhi hot (rarer) ho jati hai. Upar ki air comparatively cooler (denser) hai. Jab light upar se neeche aati hai (denser to rarer), continuously bend hoti hai aur finally TIR ho jati hai - inverted image ban jata hai paani jaisa!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Ohhhh! Matlab actually paani nahi hota, sirf inverted sky ka reflection hota hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Bilkul! ⭐ BPSC/UPSC Favorite Explanation Question! Mirage ek optical illusion hai caused by Total Internal Reflection in layers of air with different densities. Desert mein dur se paani dikhna, garam road pe shimmer - sab mirage hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Sir, optical fibre kaise kaam karta hai?"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_42_optical_fibre",
        "button_text": "Optical Fibre ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_42_optical_fibre",
      "card_slug": "card_42_optical_fibre",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "optical_fibre",
      "level": 4,
      "progress": {
        "current": 42,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Optical fibre ek thin, flexible glass/plastic fibre hai. Core (inner part, denser) surrounded by cladding (outer part, rarer). Jab light core mein enter karti hai, wo core-cladding boundary pe repeatedly TIR hoti rehti hai aur bina bahut loss ke long distances travel karti hai - even bending around corners!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Matlab light fibre ke andar zigzag bounce karti hui travel karti hai?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Exactly! Applications: (1) High-speed internet (fiber-optic cables), (2) Medical endoscopy (andar dekhne ke liye), (3) Telecommunication. ⭐ SSC/Railway Application Favorite! Optical fibres work on principle of Total Internal Reflection!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Ye toh bahut useful hai modern technology mein!"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
