      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Eye ke main parts: CORNEA (transparent front covering - max refraction yahan hoti hai!), AQUEOUS HUMOUR (liquid between cornea and lens), IRIS (colored part - controls pupil size), PUPIL (opening jahan se light enter karti hai), CRYSTALLINE LENS (convex lens - fine focusing), VITREOUS HUMOUR (jelly-like fluid), RETINA (screen jahan image banti hai - has light-sensitive cells), OPTIC NERVE (retina se brain tak signals carry karta hai)."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Itne saare parts! Sabse important kaunsa hai?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Sab important hain! Lekin RETINA crucial hai - usme ROD cells (dim light mein kaam karte hain, black-white vision) aur CONE cells (bright light mein, color vision) hote hain. ⭐ NEET Favorite - Rods for night vision, Cones for color vision!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Toh eye mein image kahan banti hai?"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_61_image_formation_eye",
        "button_text": "Image Formation ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_61_image_formation_eye",
      "card_slug": "card_61_image_formation_eye",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "eye_image_formation",
      "level": 6,
      "progress": {
        "current": 61,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Image RETINA pe banti hai - real, inverted, diminished. Lekin brain usko erect interpret karta hai! Cornea aur Lens dono milke refraction karte hain. CORNEA zyada powerful hai (fixed focal length), LENS kam powerful but ADJUSTABLE (ye power of accommodation ke liye)!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Power of accommodation matlab?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Eye lens apni focal length change kar sakta hai (ciliary muscles contract/relax karke) - ye ability hai Power of Accommodation! Door ki object dekhne ke liye lens thin (focal length zyada), paas ki object dekhne ke liye lens thick (focal length kam). ⭐ BPSC/NEET Definition Favorite!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Matlab eye automatic focus adjust kar leti hai!"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_62_near_far_point",
        "button_text": "Range Samjho ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_62_near_far_point",
      "card_slug": "card_62_near_far_point",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "near_far_point",
      "level": 6,
      "progress": {
        "current": 62,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Normal human eye ke liye: FAR POINT = INFINITY (door ki objects clearly dikh sakti hain), NEAR POINT (Least distance of distinct vision) = 25 cm (D = 25 cm). Isse paas ki object eye comfortable nahi dekh sakti - blur ho jati hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Toh 25 cm se paas ka kuch padhne ke liye magnifying glass chahiye?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Exactly! Ya fir agar eye defects hain toh spectacles. Common defects: (1) MYOPIA - door nahi dikhta (far point infinity se kam ho jata hai), (2) HYPERMETROPIA - paas nahi dikhta (near point 25 cm se zyada ho jata hai), (3) PRESBYOPIA - old age mein lens flexibility kam (both near and far problems)."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Sir myopia kaise correct karte hain?"
        }
      ],
      "navigation": {
        "next": "card_63_eye_defects",
        "button_text": "Defects Detail ➔"
      }
    },
    {
      "card_id": "card_63_eye_defects",
      "card_slug": "card_63_eye_defects",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "eye_defects",
      "level": 6,
      "progress": {
        "current": 63,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "MYOPIA (Near-sightedness): Image retina se pehle ban jata hai (eyeball elongated or lens too converging). Correction: CONCAVE LENS (diverges rays, image retina pe shift hota hai). HYPERMETROPIA (Far-sightedness): Image retina ke peeche banta hai (eyeball short or lens too weak). Correction: CONVEX LENS (converges rays, image retina pe shift)."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Toh myopia mein concave, hypermetropia mein convex yaad rakhna hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Perfect memory! ⭐ SSC/BPSC/NEET High-Frequency Matching Question! PRESBYOPIA (old age): Loss of accommodation power - both near and far affected. Correction: BIFOCAL LENS (upar concave for distant, neeche convex for near). Benjamin Franklin ne bifocal lens invent kiya!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Wow! Ek hi glass mein dono lens!"
